# API shape

Every question shows the real HTTP shape for each call. A path with no body and no response is not enough.

## Where it appears

- `README.md`, in the API section of step 1.
- `FLOW.md`, next to the chart for that feature.
- `final-design-flow.md`, next to that feature's sequence.
- The lab page, when the app is built. Each action shows the request and the response that this call actually sent. The user can read the fields. A button with no body on screen is not enough.

## Shape

Use this layout. One block per call. Comments may name an allowed value or a default.

```
POST /v1/notices -> 202 Accepted { id, status }
Body: {
  userId,
  channel,       // push | email | sms
  content,       // { title, body }
  scheduledAt    // optional, defaults to now
}
```

`push` is the phone app notification. The fields match the design this session locked. Do not invent a second path that the service does not implement.

Use 200 when the write is finished in that call. Use 202 when the call only accepts the work and a worker finishes it later. The body still returns the id and the status.

Write the notes in ASD-STE100 (`15-simplified-technical-english.mdc`). The JSON field names stay in the shape above.
